W:
W:1. Once I had a sweetheart and now I have none.
W:Once I had a sweetheart and now I have none.
W:He's gone and leave me. He's gone and leave me.
W:He's gone and leave me to sorrow and moan.
W:
W:2. Last night in sweet slumber I dreaned I did see
W:Last night in sweet slumber I dreaned I did see
W:My own precious jewel, My own precious jewel,
W:My own precious jewel sat smiling at me.
W:
W:3. And when I awakened I found it not so
W:And when I awakened I found it not so
W:My eyes like some fountain, My eyes like some fountain,
W:My eyes like some fountain with tears overflow.
W:
W:4. I'll venture through England, through France and through Spain,
W:I'll venture through England, through France and through Spain.
W:All my life I will venture, All my life I will venture,
W:All my life I will venture the watery main.
